te\n  `Zone_Growing` cells from `zoneManager.AllZones` with NO designation, and there\n  is no `sow` designation at all. The lesson taught a step that does not exist.\n- The Zzzt lesson's 800-2000 tick figure was attributed to the GAME. It is our own\n  scan cadence: `AlertsReadout.AlertCycleLength` is 24 stepped once per FRAME, so\n  vanilla re-checks in ~24 ticks at 1x. A lag we create by running fast.\n- \"A Zzzt letter means a fire is already burning\" was overstated —\n  `TryStartFireNear` can fail, and the letter text distinguishes the two cases.\n- Three weapon alerts exist, not two (`Alert_BrawlerHasRangedWeapon`).\n- SIX checklist call-shapes would have errored or read the wrong field, including\n  the most-pasted line in the corpus: `unforbid` needs `--rect:json`, because a\n  bare `--rect` autotypes to a string and returns `bad-args`. **No verb rejects an\n  unknown ARGUMENT** — unknown keys are silent, unknown values are loud — which is\n  why these were invisible.\n- Two files asserted `place-layout`'s preflight exists; spec 3.3 (`1adc737`) is\n  open and there is no `build` verb and no `place-layout` verb.\n- Three cited LINE NUMBERS, which this workspace forbids across its two decompiled\n  trees.\n\nAlso confirmed at source, so nobody re-opens it: the growing-zone potato lesson is\nnow RIGHT, deadline included. `Zone_Growing.PlantDefToGrow`'s getter assigns\n`Plant_Toxipotato` when polluted else `Plant_Potato`, and `ExposeData` SCRIBES it\n— so the first read commits the default and the deadline is real.","files":null}]}